# Scope player selectors to the active game

Restrict every post-creation player selector to the game's persisted active colours.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Board editing, Hand, Analysis Plans, and plan editing show only active colours.
- [x] All-player mode aggregates only active players.
- [x] A selection removed on SCR-007 falls back deterministically to the first active colour.
- [x] Creation from All defaults to the first active colour.
- [x] Existing Plans table content and interactions otherwise remain unchanged.
- [x] No inactive owner can be selected for new Board pieces, hands, or plans.
- [x] Selector and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Parameterized ITEM-001 and applied the active set to Board, Hand, Analysis Plans, and editors.
- Added Board-level fallback after active-player changes and first-active creation from All.
- Updated ITEM-001; the Plans table implementation itself is unchanged.
